  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Ministry of Education, Department of Higher Education. All India Survey on Higher Education (AISHE), survey rounds 2017-18 to 2021-22: the five rounds the eSankhyiki API serves. Retrieved via the MoSPI eSankhyiki API, vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>. The survey itself runs to 2010-11; earlier rounds are not chained in, because the institutional frame widened over time and a longer line would mix survey-coverage gains with genuine expansion.</p>
        <p>Coverage: all nine AISHE indicators are ingested raw; six baked bundles carry the page. The headline series (universities, colleges, enrolment, teachers, GER, GPI, PTR), the access cuts (GER by social category × gender, GPI by social category, enrolment by gender), the composition (enrolment by education level and social group), the state grain (enrolment, GER and GPI by state/UT), the faculty hierarchy (teachers by the five regular faculty types × gender) and the minority cut (PWD &amp; minority enrolment by gender). Nothing is selected away: every indicator the survey publishes is on the page or in the audit dump behind it.</p>
        <p><b>Teacher reconstruction, 2021-22.</b> The API's "All Teacher" total row is a source defect for 2021-22: All India prints 12,904 against ~1.55 million the year before, and every state cell is likewise a near-zero residual. The 2021-22 figure used here is reconstructed as the sum of the five regular faculty types (Professor &amp; Equivalent, Reader &amp; Associate Professor, Lecturer/Assistant Professor, Demonstrator/Tutor, Temporary Teacher): a sum equal to 99.0–99.2% of the published total in every clean year. Earlier years use the published "All Teacher" total as served. The raw, defective value is preserved in the audit dump.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions &amp; uncertainty</h6>
        <p>AISHE results are final on release. The five rounds are comparable by design but are never chained into a spliced index. Enrolment counts enrolments, not distinct students; GER divides by a population projection; GPI is a ratio of ratios. Where the data carry a known defect (the 2021-22 teacher total), the reconstruction is disclosed and the raw value is kept. Where something is not measured, completion, dropout, learning, this guide says so.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Education, version 1.1, adds GER by gender (§07), the state enrolment companion strip (§08), the education-level small multiples (§09), the faculty-hierarchy plate (§10) and the PWD &amp; minority plate (§11). Next scheduled revision: on release of the 2022-23 round.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
